    "  - Fork bombs and malicious patterns",
    "  - Destructive permission changes (chmod/chown)",
    "  - Force-pushing to main/master branches",
    "  - Hard git resets and aggressive cleanup",
    "  - Piped deletions (| xargs rm, find -delete)",
    "  - COMPOUND BLOCKS (NEW): All dangerous ops chained with &&",
    "    - '* && rm -rf *', '* && sudo *', '* && chmod -R 000 *'",
    "    - '* && git push --force *', '* && git reset --hard *'",
    "    - 'rm * && *', 'sudo * && *' (dangerous commands first)",
    "  - Writing to system directories (/etc, /usr, ~/.ssh)",
    "  - Writing to read-only NanoAOD data (/publicfs/cms/data/)",
    "",
    "ALLOW RULES (Workflow operations):",
    "  - Read/Edit/Write within project directory",
    "  - Job management (hep_q, condor_q/rm)",
    "  - Git operations (except force-push to protected branches)",
    "  - Python/bash analysis scripts",
    "  - File operations (mkdir, cp, mv, tar)",
    "  - COMPOUND COMMANDS: Bash(* && *) allows all safe chains",
    "    - Examples: 'git add && git commit', 'mkdir dir && cd dir'",
    "    - 'python3 script.py && echo done'",
    "  - Piped commands for analysis (grep, awk, wc, etc.)",
    "",
    "SAFETY PHILOSOPHY:",
    "  1. Deny rules take priority - dangerous ops blocked even if pattern matches allow",
    "  2. Generic compound pattern (Bash(* && *)) provides flexibility",
    "  3. Strengthened deny rules catch dangerous combinations",
    "  4. Read-only access to system data directories",
    "  5. Git safety: protect main branches, allow normal operations",
    "  6. Regular commits provide rollback capability",
    "",
